{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/131432-imhotep-stats-from-the-mummy-movies","id":131432,"title":"Imhotep stats from the mummy movies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-10T20:08:00-07:00","id":131432,"title":"Imhotep stats from the mummy movies","content":"I haven't received my Mummy the Curse book yet but, I was thinking what Imhotep's stats would be? From skimming the preview of Mummy at Drivethrurpg, I'm sure he'd have those Sand Utterances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2720-theoctopusman","name":"theoctopusman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T20:44:16-07:00","id":131485,"title":"","content":"I tried to stat him up once. I figured he'd be a Su-mement since he functioned as a priest, but I suppose an Arisen of any guild could pose as different positions over the millennia. You could argue he's a Scribe because I think his relic could be the Book of the Dead, but it could just be a non-relic tome with a 'mortal sorcerer' spell that lets you awaken a Mummy. I don't think he has any special powers to resurrect people as an utterance, because reviving his dead girlfriend is more like a 'plot power via GM fiat.'<br /> <br /> I would give him the Jar of Teeth utterance from <i>Guildhalls of the Deathless</i> to represent his special connection to his canopic jars. Maybe he'd also have Entombed Glory affinity since he mostly performs his rituals in his tomb, so he might have more power there. And as you said, he'd have Wrathful Desert Power.<br /> <br /> So besides Jar of Teeth, Wrathful Desert Power, and Entombed Glory, I think you could kind of go with anything. Being able to activate as many tiers of those utterances as possible, though, of course implies certain Pillar values","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T21:09:32-07:00","id":131528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/131432-imhotep-stats-from-the-mummy-movies?p=131485#post131485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think he has any special powers to resurrect people as an utterance, because reviving his dead girlfriend is more like a 'plot power via GM fiat.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. It works almost exactly like the second tier of Words of Dead Glory. He also resurrects a bunch of skeletal soldiers and mummified priests. The former act a bit like Awakened Servants, while the latter are almost certainly Nenitu.<br /> <br /> That said, Wrathful Desert Power is definitely a thing, and his position as high priest certainly lends itself towards regarding him as a Su-Menent. If you want to treat the curses he inflicts on Egypt during the first movie as his powers, then he almost certainly has Secrets Ripped From Skies, as there is a meteor shower at one point. Mind you, if you go that route, he sports a staggering number of Utterances by the end (Dreams of Dead Gods for the chanting cultists/the constant opposition by generations of the same bloodlines is one, the water turning into blood is another, the scarab beetles a third, and so on).<br /> <br /> But personally, I would give him Words of Dead Glory, Wrathful Desert Power, and Secrets as his Utterances. For his Affinities, I agree that Entombed Glory seems fitting. I'd be inclined to give him the heart-eating Bane Affinity as well (can't recall the name). And probably Guardian Wrath/Dominating Might, going by the way he throws mortals around the place.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's a thought. The way he sucks the life from foes gives me a definite Shuankhsen feel (not to mention the way he was killed, more punishment than reward).<br /> <br /> Oh, and I wouldn't bother giving him any dots in Languages, but five points in Tomb Geometry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T00:47:43-07:00","id":131762,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I remember thinking he'd have something to summon up mindless zombie-skeletons but I didn't want to overload him on utterances, like you realized too. Also, Guardian Wrath and Dominating Might were also affinities I considered for that very reason.<br /> <br /> His punishment I guess I didn't consider his 'true' origin, if he's 'really' a <i>Mummy: the Curse</i> Mummy, similar to his guild. His movie background states he was a priest, but that could've been a guise he maintained during an early Sothic turn; or, indeed, it could imply he's Su-menent. Likewise, the punishment of eaten-alive-by-scarabs might have been how that particular Descent ended rather than his origin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:19:38-07:00","id":132909,"title":"","content":"Imhotep in the films was a priest, but to be historically accurate to who Imhotep was irl, I made him a Mason--outside of the movies, he was the guy who designed pyramids, mapped the sekhem and medicine of the human body, etc. Likewise, I gave him severely low memory in 1920/30, to explain why hes confused about ankh sun amon and his own birthdate, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}